  "query_preview": "it through 8 PM Sunday. \n\nThrough Sunday, temperatures are expected to trend upward \nthrough the upper 90s, as dewpoints trend a bit lower each day. \nSo, it is possible we see some triple digit temperatures over \nthe weekend, while heat indices may struggle to climb above 105.\nRegardless, this will be at least a week long extreme heat \nevent, so the Warning will be worthwhile even if a few locations\ndon't quite reach 105 over the weekend.\n\nThe upper ridge retreats to the south early next week, but\nsouthern portions of the Quad State could still see high\ntemperatures in the middle 90s and heat indices may reach the\ntriple digits again Monday. Highs will remain above normal,\nalbeit in the lower and middle 90s through Wednesday. \n\nPrecipitation chances will come in from the north late Sunday \nnight and especially Monday afternoon. Intermittent 15% PoPs \nwill then linger through Tuesday and into Wednesday. Confidence\nin coverage and timing of precipitation early next week is very\nlow.",
